Revision history for ITM

{{$NEXT}}
    - The type method of ITM::Sync, ITM::Overflow, ITM::Instrumentation and
      ITM::HardwareSource returns the type constant instead of dying with
      "Undefined subroutine"; the constants now exist before the packet
      classes are loaded
    - itm_parse croaks on an empty input, naming the missing header byte,
      instead of returning an ITM::Overflow packet with uninitialized-value
      warnings
    - itm_parse called with a header hashref and a payload leaves the
      caller's header untouched; it used to remove the size key
    - Every module carries its own version, enables strict and warnings and
      has an abstract; the hand-written SUPPORT sections are gone, the
      release generates them (IRC channel #hardware)
    - The distribution builds: add LICENSE, README.md and Changes; the
      cpanfile names the modules the code loads (Carp, Exporter, Moo) and
      drops the zero version pin
